  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A black iron cauldron with a dent in its rim, older than the kingdom it was found in. It is warm before any fire is lit under it, and it has never once boiled over.</p><p><strong>Serve the Feast.</strong> Once per day, over an hour of cooking with nothing but water, the cauldron serves @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplHeroesFeas]{Heroes' Feast} for up to twelve. It can do so again after the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Nobody Leaves Hungry.</strong> On any day when it has not served its feast, the cauldron will feed plain stew to as many people as come to it, a village or an army, until the last of them is full. It has never been known to do this for anyone who meant to sell the food.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
